WEBVTT

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:15.240
Training with Rin-san, huh?

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.070
What's she like anyway?

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.330
She drew out Hayato and Prontea,
and taught them how to fight.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:28.960
<b>#2
The
Black
 South</b>

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.100
She's also a survivor of the Idaten who 
battled the demons 800 years ago.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.960
The only living being to truly understand
 the demonic involvement of the past.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:32.490
She's the strongest Idaten
 in current existence.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.220
If we're going to learn how to fight, 
she's the best person to turn to.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.720
Plus, at the moment, it's dangerous to be 
apart from either her or Hayato.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.190
According to Hayato, 
that doctor was a robot...

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.290
We can assume whoever was controlling it

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.230
is now in possession of all the data 
it collected during our battle.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.900
Suppose they have a minion even more 
powerful than that demonic beast,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.240
and it were to attack.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.800
We'd be done for.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.390
If we stick with Hayato and Rin-san 
under the premise of training,

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.490
we can probably avoid getting done in.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:02.920
Probably?

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.320
Well, the plan doesn't preclude the 
possibly of getting killed by Rin-san...

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.250
To be honest, I'm not thrilled about this.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.770
I used to train alongside Hayato,

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.670
<i>At the time, I thought to myself,
 "What's the big deal?"</i>

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:16.770
and as embarrassing as it is to admit,

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.630
it was so harsh that
 I turned tail after three months.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.010
<i>"Why is Ysley exaggerating so much?"</i>

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.010
I haven't seen Rin-san since.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.020
Time to die, you old—

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.720
Just as brutal as I remember.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:15.520
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:31.980
<b><i>The Idaten Deities
</i>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hKnow Only Peace</b>

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.510
What... What was that?! You call that training?
 It looked like a beating!

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:47.990
Well, er, theoretically. 
It's the proper way to train an Idaten, but...

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.820
<i>The problem is that Rin-san 
doesn't understand the theory.</i>

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.390
<i>She's just doing what she wants.</i>

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.080
<i>And that's terrifying!</i>

00:03:55.080 --> 00:04:00.090
Come on, Ysley. Wouldn't it be safer 
to go learn from Prontea-san?

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.510
She vanished!

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:10.430
Well, well... We meet again, Ysley.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:14.690
It's been, what, fifty years? 
And you have the nerve to show up now?

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.780
<i>What's with this unbelievable bloodlust?!</i>

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.150
<i>Shit. She's even angrier than I anticipated.</i>

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.590
<i>The wrong answer here means death,</i>

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:29.270
<i>and no excuse will be enough 
to make a difference.</i>

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.410
<i>That being the case...</i>

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.620
<i>I have only one option!</i>

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.080
Rin-san!

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.530
I can't deny that I ran 
from your training once before,

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:42.670
and I know how presumptuous 
it may seem after all this time,

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.380
but please teach me how to fight again!

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.330
<i>Ysley took the direct approach.</i>

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.390
<b>D
I
R
E
C
T</b>

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:51.140
<i>He straightforwardly, without pretense,
 asked for what he wanted,</i>

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.140
<b>D
I
R
E
C
T</b>

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.840
<i>which effectively served
to mask his true intentions.</i>

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.410
<b>True Intentions</b>

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:55.520
<b>Mask</b>

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.520
<i>And it was super effective.</i>

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.900
<i>To Rin, who was driven by her
sense of duty to fight demons,</i>

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.940
<i>an Idaten who shirked his training 
in order to learn in the human world</i>

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.410
<i>was essentially the same as a shut-in 
who did nothing but play porn games all day.</i>

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:14.660
<i>But when Ysley spoke, it was as if</i>

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.580
<i>that sort of fail-son suddenly 
put on a business suit...</i>

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.450
I'm so sorry for everything 
I put you through!

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:23.110
Starting today, I'm going to turn 
over a new leaf and look for a job!

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.680
<i>And the degree to which this affected Rin
was not unlike that of a mother.</i>

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:33.010
I see, I see! So you've 
finally realized your duty!

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.810
Oh, Grandfather! I've never been happier!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.190
Now then, Ysley, who's the girl?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.930
Oh, right. This is a new Idaten...

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.070
My name is Paula. It's nice to meet you.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.570
Really? Did you draw her out?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:51.160
Or was it Hayato?

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.080
Oh, no, I was drawn out by Prontea-san.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.330
<b>"Drawing Out"</b>

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.330
<i>Idaten are naturally occurring entities.</i>

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:02.200
<i>If they are left alone, they will still 
manifest within a few centuries.</i>

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.130
<i>But with the intervention of another Idaten,</i>

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.340
<i>they can be drawn out in an instant.</i>

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:11.250
<i>Those drawn out in this fashion often take</i>

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.930
<i>the Idaten responsible as their master.</i>

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.100
<i>This is why Rin, 
who spends nearly all her time</i>

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:18.400
<i>where the demons have been sealed,</i>

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.370
<i>will occasionally travel 
across the world with Hayato.</i>

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:25.900
<i>She means to find and draw out
new Idaten to join her.</i>

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.710
Oh, Prontea, eh?

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:29.260
That takes me back.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:32.760
It took me 200 years to
 train him into shape.

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:37.620
Of all my students, he's the only one 
I'd say can stand on his own two feet.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.290
So, are you here to train, as well?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.320
<i>I still regret it to this day.</i>

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.050
Well, that's what I was thinking of.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:51.300
<i>Why didn't I just say no
and run away back then?</i>

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:53.930
Very well.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.400
Come at me, then.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.660
<i>What? Already?</i>

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.600
<i>Well, since we're just getting started, 
I should probably take it easy—</i>

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:11.910
Rest in peace.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.050
Well, she's certainly fragile.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:22.880
What in the world did Prontea teach her?

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.160
<i>Probably nothing in terms of combat...</i>

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.840
Well then, Ysley, let's see what you've got.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.590
C-Certainly. 
Pleasure to be working with you...

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.610
You still alive, Paula?

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.240
<i>Can't talk, huh? 
Probably a punctured lung, I'd wager.</i>

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.050
I can't believe the dumb old bitch 
just chucked me like that!

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.960
My face still smarts.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:02.740
Hey, it's Ysley and Paula. 
What brings you guys around?

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:05.080
Finally decide to start training?

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:09.180
Oh, damn, is Paula almost dead?

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.020
She won't be able to move 
for three days, I'd say.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:14.430
You never hold back, do you?

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.540
Well, don't sweat it.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:21.560
You get your organs mashed up enough, 
you stop worrying about it eventually.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.000
Okay, Hayato, we're sparring again.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:27.810
What, already?

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.930
Ysley, you're up again in two hours.

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:40.850
<i>I hadn't abandoned my training
with her previously just because it was harsh.</i>

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:44.540
<i>I couldn't accept that this daily routine</i>

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.220
<i>would amount to any real growth.</i>

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:55.430
Why is it that we Idaten know our names 
at the moment of our manifestation?

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:58.430
Couldn't say. It's a good question, though.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.120
How does the drawing out 
process work, anyway?

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.840
How exactly do we appear in nature?

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:08.710
It should be impossible for organisms 
to simply appear from nothing.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.570
We're gods, so doesn't that explain it?

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.660
Then, as deities, why do we 
have human appearances,

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.120
manifest wearing human clothing,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.440
and communicate with human language?

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:22.040
No clue.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:28.280
<i>I also thought talking to her
 was a waste of time.</i>

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:37.460
<b>Zoble Military
Front Line</b>

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:42.310
We are not waging a defensive war.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.020
We espouse no lukewarm ideology, either.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.480
This is an invasion, plain and simple.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.020
Now, tell me what you want!

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.420
We want to kill, ma'am!

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:51.710
We want to steal, ma'am!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.100
We want to spoil, ma'am!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.570
Who do you want to kill?

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.210
Our enemies, ma'am!

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:57.650
What do you want to steal?!

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.110
Their wealth, ma'am!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.700
And what do you want to spoil?!

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.730
The finest girl I can find, ma'am!

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:03.620
Virgins, ma'am!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:04.920
Little girls, yeah!

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:05.400
A housewife in front of her husband!

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.400
Shotas!

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.450
A beefy older gent, ma'am!

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.530
Too far, dude! Unbelievable!

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:10.960
I respect your candor. Permission granted.

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.460
The land and resources will belong to Zoble!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.590
Everything else is your reward.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.300
Pillage to your heart's content, you dogs!

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.220
Charge!

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:28.360
I have a report, ma'am.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:32.510
All C-Soldiers are to return 
to base immediately.

00:10:32.510 --> 00:10:35.400
There was an emergency 
notification from Dr. Obami.

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:38.400
From the De... the doctor, you say?

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:40.810
Yes, ma'am. What shall we do?

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.790
Requesting a return in the 
middle of a battle like this...

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.980
It's fine. I'll be the only one returning.

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.800
The outcome of this battle 
was a foregone conclusion.

00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:54.010
By the way, I'd take a few 
steps back if I were you.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.420
There's a missile headed this way.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:01.840
What... General?!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.390
General!

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.180
Direct hit confirmed!

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.770
Did we take out General Piscalat?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:19.160
Reload immediately! 
Fire as soon as the target is—

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.540
Idiots.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:32.580
Ready a jet for me. 
I leave the rest in your hands.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.790
Take <i>everything</i>.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.210
Ma'am! Understood!

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.650
All right, that should do for today.

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:50.940
Okay...

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:55.680
Come on, guys. Let's go hang out. 
Can you move yet?

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.320
Dead...

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.320
<b>D</b>

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.320
<b>D</b>

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.320
<b>E</b>

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.320
<b>A</b>

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.210
Dying... Gonna die...

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:03.570
Paula, your eyes are doing 
some kinda fish thing!

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:07.430
Ysley, is there really any 
purpose to this training?

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:09.690
Are you sure it's not just torture?

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:13.580
I wondered the same thing for a time.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:17.540
But there is a proper logic to it,
 so rest assured.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.610
What the hell's logic 
got to do with training?

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:23.460
You fight every day, 
you're bound to get stronger.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:28.710
Honestly, I envy your 
simplistic outlook, Hayato.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:31.290
Wouldn't most people
turn to weight training instead?

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:35.140
That said, weight training 
would be pointless for Idaten.

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.440
Since we've got nothing to do until 
we're healed, I might as well explain...

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:41.690
Don't care. Your explanations 
are too confusing.

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:45.340
It's okay. I'll hear you out.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.450
Did you have to make it sound so pitiful?

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:48.950
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:50.110
We Idaten are different on a
 cellular level from all other organisms,

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:49.950
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.030
including humans.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:50.950
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:52.050
Hence the unique training.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:51.950
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:53.440
Consider how we can survive 
having our hearts crushed.

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:52.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.500
Rin-san believes our 
supernatural nature explains this,

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:53.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:54.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:56.330
but demons die easily when 
<i>their</i> hearts are crushed.

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:55.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.460
See, the destruction of the heart 
stops the circulatory system,

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:56.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:57.480 --> 00:12:57.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.770
halting the delivery of oxygen and nutrients.

00:12:58.480 --> 00:12:58.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:59.480 --> 00:12:59.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:01.400
This is where we differ from living creatures.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:00.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.370
We require no nutrition
 and don't really need to breathe,

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:01.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:02.960
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.510
thus a lack of circulating 
blood is no problem.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:03.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:04.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:05.960
Though we act short of breath when tired,

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:05.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:07.120
this is more a "habit" than anything else—

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:06.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:07.820
a habit of living creatures.

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:07.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:08.850
Our genesis lies in the 
thoughts of living creatures,

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:08.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.940
and our creation is dictated by them.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:09.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.500
The reason we have human forms
 rather than anything else

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:10.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:11.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.130
is that humans have considerably
more thoughts than other creatures.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:12.970
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:15.160
The reason you specifically are able 
to speak with birds is because

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:13.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:14.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.160
you're partly composed of bird thoughts.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:15.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:16.760
Now then,

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:16.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.380
what does any of this have to do
 with torturous training?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:17.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:19.480
Hayato was actually right.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:18.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.770
The more your organs are destroyed,
 the less it bothers you.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:19.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:20.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.320
His body is already become
something distinctly inhuman.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:21.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.890
In exchange, he's gained something
that living creatures do not have:

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:22.980
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:23.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:25.860
a metamorphosis which makes 
him more effective in combat.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:24.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:25.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.800
The kind of evolution we undergo
 is tied to our own thoughts.

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:26.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:27.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:30.090
Wanting to be stronger, 
have more resilience, et cetera...

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:28.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:29.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.090
And the most efficient way to 
force these changes is to expose

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:30.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:31.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:32.990
the body to extreme stimuli.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:32.990
<b>Fast Forward Explanation in Progress</b>

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.000
So how long does that all take?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.250
Somewhere between fifty to a hundred years.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.250
Sorry. Not happening.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:48.610
Come to think of it, why would you suddenly 
start such nuts and bolts training?

00:13:48.610 --> 00:13:52.760
Did seeing a demon in person suddenly
make you realize your responsibility?

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.770
Is that what it looks like, Paula?

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:06.030
<i>That's the face he makes when he's 
got something really nasty in mind...</i>

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:10.530
Hey, Granny, what's that?

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.410
What's what?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.430
You've got something on your clothes.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:15.720
Some tiny metal thing.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:18.160
What is this?

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.380
Some kinda machine, maybe?

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:23.390
What's it doing on you, though?

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:24.420
I have no idea.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:29.340
C'mon, what'd you have to break it for? 
Ysley might've been able to figure it out.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:33.390
Doesn't matter. Once it's broken, 
it's not anything anymore, is it?

00:14:34.030 --> 00:14:35.830
Yeah, guess not.

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.270
<i>Oh, but it was.</i>

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.990
<b>Gend Autonomous Zone Invaded and Occupied by Zoble Forces</b>

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:52.360
Paula, remember how I told you we're born 
from the thoughts of living creatures?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.920
The thing is, thoughts alone 
don't make us manifest.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.000
It takes an additional element...

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.130
A desire for salvation.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.980
It's okay. Don't be scared.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.540
Dear God...

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.190
Please, God...

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:25.390
Please... grant us salvation...

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:26.480
God!

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.490
That doesn't make any sense, though.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:36.690
You said human desire for salvation 
is what makes Idaten appear,

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:39.960
but we don't help humans at all.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:45.090
That's not so strange. It's other humans 
who make humans suffer in war, right?

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:49.210
What sense would it make 
to fight humans to save humans?

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.590
I guess you're right...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.250
Two human nations fight, 
and one is destroyed...

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:59.220
The victor grows in its place, 
so it's not a problem.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:02.800
It's not as if the humans care about how 
the composition of a forest might change

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:04.730
as long as there are still plants there.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:08.030
And if an invasive species wipes 
out the native wildlife of a lake,

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:10.240
they'd just think of it 
as a good fishing spot.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.060
This is all to say that, 
while we're in a different position,

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:16.500
our thought process isn't 
so different from the humans'.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:21.500
Still, there's a condition under which
we will fight to protect them.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.400
Consider the demons...

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:29.070
For example, say you happened upon that Gyudo
monster attacking some humans.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:32.020
If you were as powerful as Rin-san,
 what would you do?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.010
I think I'd get rid of him.

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:38.840
Yet why would you help humans 
that you normally just ignore?

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.990
Huh, that's a good question...
 I wonder.

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:45.380
I guess because I'd feel
 compelled to fight the monster?

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.840
Wrong. It's because if you do nothing,
the humans would be wiped out.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:53.020
Humans are similar. If a forest they 
normally don't care about catches on fire,

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.030
they'll make an effort to put it out.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:58.660
But right now, mankind is distinctly 
<i>not</i> on the brink of destruction.

00:16:59.050 --> 00:17:00.490
They're prosperous enough

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:03.950
to kill one another for simple 
self-interest, of all things.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.630
And as humans engage in pointless 
wars to amuse themselves,

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.050
the collective thoughts of those
 caught in the crossfire

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:14.550
is what calls us forth... to do nothing.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.550
Thus we do nothing.

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:20.720
I suppose you could say we're a generation 
of Idaten deities who only know peace.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.710
<i>Is there no God after all?</i>

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:36.320
Still, there's something I don't understand.
 What purpose do the demons serve?

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:37.830
Did you know, Paula?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:42.330
If left uncontested, 
they'd continue to predate and destroy

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.850
until the world was completely barren

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:48.330
and they ultimately died from starvation.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.950
It doesn't make any sense.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:55.340
If there are any intelligent 
demons out there...

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.890
I would love to ask what they want.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.770
Hey! Pi-chan, Pi-chan!

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:08.270
Long time no see! 
You been doin' good, yeah?

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:11.150
It's been a few years since 
I last saw you, right? Right?!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.000
<i>The way she talks is still annoying.</i>

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:15.110
Nickel!

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:18.150
You need to show more respect 
to a superior officer!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.660
Come to think of it, you're right!

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.790
I need'st be formal with my manner 
of speech, do I not, General Piscalat?!

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.790
How'd she survive a fall from that height?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:36.290
Putting that aside, this meeting 
should be of incredible import!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:40.300
I dare say we're in for the first 
meeting of substance in quite some time!

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.230
Your Majesty,

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:48.730
<b>Prime Minister of the Zoble Empire
Biarov</b>

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:48.730
why am I not a part of this meeting?

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.370
Because it has nothing to do with you.

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:55.460
<b>Emperor of the Zoble Empire
Takeshita</b>

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:55.460
<b>Empress
Brandy</b>

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:54.290
That's right. Your job is running 
the government, isn't it?

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:57.240
Just focus on policy and diplomacy.

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:00.810
<i>What the hell kind of diplomacy could a 
war-mongering nation like this manage?</i>

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:03.370
As you wish, ma'am.

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:07.380
Hey there, Your Majesty the Emperor!

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:11.780
You're looking as miserable as ever!

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:15.100
We'll be waiting in the
 meeting room! Bye-bye!

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:19.710
I must say, formal language is most tiring,
 don't you think, General Piscalat?!

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:21.340
You're not even pulling it off.

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:24.540
Nickel certainly seems to be in high spirits.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:26.070
We should get going ourselves.

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:27.700
Yes, I suppose we should.

00:19:29.630 --> 00:19:33.850
<i>This meeting was called by Obami,
 head of weapons development...</i>

00:19:33.850 --> 00:19:36.930
<i>What is that madman's game now?</i>

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:37.940
Kagekiki.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.570
Sir?

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.190
I want you to look into this.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:43.070
By your command.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.070
<b>Meeting Room</b>

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:47.290
<b>Commander of the Zoble Imperial Navy
Neput</b>

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:47.290
<b>Child Soldier
Cory</b>

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.000
<b>Zoble Army Defense Force Soldier
G-Thirteen</b>

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.000
<b>The Lively Chief Clerk
of Childcare Support
Barcode</b>

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.000
<b>Star Midwife
Umeyo</b>

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:52.250
<b>Animal Trainer
Miku</b>

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.500
<b>And everybody else</b>

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.550
Is that everyone?

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:57.500
The doctor's not here yet.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:20:01.630
<b>PM Biarov's Personal Agent
Kagekiki the Ninja</b>

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:01.630
<i>What a bizarre assemblage...</i>

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.950
<i>What do they mean to discuss?</i>

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.930
Sorry about the delay, folks.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.940
<b>Head of Weapons Development
Doctor Obami</b>

00:20:09.380 --> 00:20:11.940
Let's get this meeting underway.

00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:19.250
What happened to you...?

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:24.160
Shut it! My usual body got 
wrecked by that Idaten brat!

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:27.060
<i>His "usual body"? It was wrecked?</i>

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:29.540
<i>And what exactly is an Idaten?</i>

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:33.840
Granted, that's part of why 
we're having this meeting.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:35.810
First, let's start with...

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:38.110
Oh, can I take care of one thing first?

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:39.420
What is it, Nickel?

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:50.720
Would you look at that!
If isn't Kagekiki-kun!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.730
Look, I understand being curious...

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:56.730
But eavesdropping is just rude!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:01.780
Oh, sorry about that, Take-kun.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.700
Try to be more careful.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.530
Now, we're ready when you are...

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:13.540
O great Demon Lord who granted 
us human forms and intelligence.

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:17.480
All right, let's start by reviewing 
the footage of the Idaten.
